    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0277" n="145" xml:id="pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> Leahy Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 121 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Truman
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d121-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-04">4 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Prime Minister to President Truman. Personal and secret. Number 103.</p>
                <p>As we are all agreed that the press should not be allowed at <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Terminal</hi> I think that it would be advantageous
                    to announce this publicly in advance. This will avoid disappointment and the
                    sending to Berlin of high powered press representatives. I suggest we should
                    each let it be known that they will not be allowed at <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Terminal</hi> and that all that will be issued will
                    be official communiqués as may be decided from time to time.</p>
                <p>I am sending a similar telegram to Stalin.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d121-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d121-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d121-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d121-f2" n="2" xml:id="d121-f2-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic"> Stalin’s Correspondence</hi>, vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 371. Stalin accepted Churchill’s
                    suggestion in a message of July 6. See <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p.
                    372.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
